    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "H1N1A4",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the full adder: first XOR stage of half adder 1 (chain 4 of 4), Y = NAND(A, B), feeding H1N24.B. The whole full adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of A, B and Cin onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_cf0798e49f534aedb6bf60ebdef591a3",
        "IdGuid": "d27bad24-6f34-48e7-923a-d50b54e11014",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "6767b1e5-254a-43ca-abda-9e9a9ae271fa",
